# Paths the "Autopilot merge" workflow never merges: a PR touching any of them waits for Farouk.
# One bash pattern per line, matched against the whole repo-relative path (`*` also matches `/`).
# The workflow reads this file from main, so a PR cannot loosen the rules it is checked against.
# docs/AUTOPILOT.md describes the same list in words.
#
# Farouk, 2026-11-16 (OTA-202): everything else merges on its own once CI is green and the Fable
# reviews have no Critical (migrations: db-migration-checker; workflows, dependencies, .claude/,
# CLAUDE.md, scripts, configs, deploy files: security-reviewer). Only the merge gate itself stays
# here, so the autopilot can never change the rule that checks its own PRs.

.github/autopilot-protected-paths
.github/workflows/autopilot-merge.yml
